    "preamble": "Meeravali Shaik vs The State Of Ap on 6 March, 2025 Aphc010101982025 In The High Court Of Andhra Pradesh At Amaravati [ 3457 ] (Special Original Jurisdiction) THURSDAY, THE SIXTH DAY OF MARCH TWO THOUSAND AND TWENTY FIVE PRESENT THE HONOURABLE SRI JUSTICE HARINATH.N",
    "facts": "3. It is alleged that the accused No.1 has purchased the prohibited noxious food items from accused No.2 and that they were selling the same without license to the public.",
    "arguments": "2. The learned counsel for the petitioners submits that the petitioners are arraigned as accused Nos.1 and 2 in C.C.No.120 of 2019 on the file of Additional Judicial Magistrate of First Class, Addanki. 4. It is submitted that though the petitioners are charged with the offence of purchasing noxious food items and selling them without permission, the police have registered the case and filed charge sheet for the offences under Sections 353, 420, 273, 188 r/w 34 IPC and Sections 58, 59 and 63 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 5. The learned counsel for the petitioners submits that the police do not have the jurisdiction to Meeravali Shaik vs The State Of Ap on 6 March, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/89862213/ 1 register the case under the provisions of Penal Code and that similar matters came up for consideration before this Court in the batch of quash petitions, which were decided by this Court in Criminal Petition No.3731 of 2018 and batch vide order dated 27.08.2018. 6.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "2. The learned counsel for the petitioners submits that the petitioners are arraigned as accused Nos.1 and 2 in C.C.No.120 of 2019 on the file of Additional Judicial Magistrate of First Class, Addanki. 4. It is submitted that though the petitioners are charged with the offence of purchasing noxious food items and selling them without permission, the police have registered the case and filed charge sheet for the offences under Sections 353, 420, 273, 188 r/w 34 IPC and Sections 58, 59 and 63 of Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 5. The learned counsel for the petitioners submits that the police do not have the jurisdiction to Meeravali Shaik vs The State Of Ap on 6 March, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/89862213/ 1 register the case under the provisions of Penal Code and that similar matters came up for consideration before this Court in the batch of quash petitions, which were decided by this Court in Criminal Petition No.3731 of 2018 and batch vide order dated 27.08.2018. 6.",
